<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of the Angrivarian Wall</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">16 CE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of the Angrivarian Wall was fought in 16 CE between Roman legions under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germanicus">Germanicus</a> and Germanic tribes led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arminius">Arminius</a> of the Cherusci. According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tacitus">Tacitus</a>, the Germans held an earthwork built by the Angrivarii on their border with the Cherusci, but the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> stormed it. Coming soon after the victory at Idistaviso, it ended Germanicus's campaigns, as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiberius">Tiberius</a> recalled him the following year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-angrivarian-wall.jpg" alt="Battle of the Angrivarian Wall" width="320" height="255" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cristiano64 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Germania_16_Germanico.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
